🚀 What you need

There are 2 things:

ArgoCD CLI (argocd) → run commands from your machine
ArgoCD Server (in Kubernetes) → actual GitOps engine

👉 You need both

🧠 Official documentation (use these)
ArgoCD install: https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/getting_started/
CLI install: https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/cli_installation/
🖥️ PART 1 — Install ArgoCD CLI
✅ Linux
curl -sSL -o argocd \
https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64

chmod +x argocd

sudo mv argocd /usr/local/bin/

Test:

argocd version
✅ Windows (Git Bash)

👉 Best way (simple and clean):

curl -sSL -o /c/bin/argocd.exe \
https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-windows-amd64.exe

Then:

Create folder:
C:\bin
Add to PATH:
Search “Environment Variables”
Add C:\bin

Test in Git Bash:

argocd version
